DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
23644::$$$message_0180_0000_0000$$$::   "I want to save you," she said.[lr]::
23645::$$$message_0180_0000_0001$$$::She was sincere, without a hint of doubt, when she told me tearfully that she wanted to free me from my suffering.::
23646::$$$message_0180_0001_0000$$$::All I felt in that moment was pessimism.[lr]::
23647::$$$message_0180_0001_0001$$$::I wasn't happy or grateful that she came to save me.[lr]::
23648::$$$message_0180_0001_0002$$$::Her kindness was misguided. A burden, even.[lr]::
23649::$$$message_0180_0001_0003$$$::I couldn't quite bring myself to feel hatred, but to be frank, I wanted her to go back to her own world.::
23650::$$$message_0180_0002_0000$$$::It's not that I hated her.[lr]::
23651::$$$message_0180_0002_0001$$$::But her motivation was entirely off base. She should have known that there was no saving anyone.[lr]::
23652::$$$message_0180_0002_0002$$$::In the first place, [l]she knew that she had no way to save me.::
23653::$$$message_0180_0003_0000$$$::"                  "[lr]::
23654::$$$message_0180_0003_0001$$$::I answer her in a voice that doesn't quite come out.[lr]::
23655::$$$message_0180_0003_0002$$$::I can't form any words because my throat is crushed, so I try to shake my head, but remember I can't even do that.[lr]::
23656::$$$message_0180_0003_0003$$$::In the end, she gave up and returned to the earth.[lr]::
23657::$$$message_0180_0003_0004$$$::She kept trying for days, until she finally realized that she was just talking to a dead husk.::
23658::$$$message_0180_0004_0000$$$::   That happened, apparently.[lr]::
23659::$$$message_0180_0004_0001$$$::Right now, I'm feeling an emotion similar to recalling something I can't remember.[lr]::
23660::$$$message_0180_0004_0002$$$::Doubt and compassion.[lr]::
23661::$$$message_0180_0004_0003$$$::That finicky woman feels obliged to me, even though she doesn't have any definite reason to be.::
23662::$$$message_0180_0005_0000$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz.[lr]::
23663::$$$message_0180_0005_0001$$$::The woman who became Avenger's Master directs the same misguided feelings as she did that other time.::
23664::$$$message_0180_0006_0000$$$::"Ha[wvl][se storage=se201.wav]...haah, [wvl][shock vmax=20 time=1400 count=12]haa, hah...!"[lr]::
23665::$$$message_0180_0006_0001$$$::I push my heart five times more than usual, finally reaching that dilapidated house.[lr]::
23666::$$$message_0180_0006_0002$$$::My throat's on fire.[lr]::
23667::$$$message_0180_0006_0003$$$::My right leg is in tatters, after forcing it to sprint beyond repair.[lr]::
23668::$$$message_0180_0006_0004$$$::I've used up nearly all the magical energy Bazett was giving me, and I'm nearly physically exhausted.[lr]::
23669::$$$message_0180_0006_0005$$$::Basically, I'm running on fumes, so he can do whatever he wants to me.[wdash canskip=0]::
23670::$$$message_0180_0007_0000$$$::"What are you doing? Run this way, Avenger!"[lr]::
23671::$$$message_0180_0007_0001$$$::One step ahead, Bazett turns back from the house towards me.[lr]::
23672::$$$message_0180_0007_0002$$$::"Hah... Haah, haah, hah... Got it!"[lr]::
23673::$$$message_0180_0007_0003$$$::Using both hands, [se storage=se192.wav]I scramble inside on all fours.[lr]::
23674::$$$message_0180_0007_0004$$$::The door shuts behind me.[lr]::
23675::$$$message_0180_0007_0005$$$::It may as well be plywood to that monster, but it's necessary for our mental health.::
23676::$$$message_0180_0008_0000$$$::"[wacky len=12]"[lr]::
23677::$$$message_0180_0008_0001$$$::...I hear a roar.[lr]::
23678::$$$message_0180_0008_0002$$$::The giant monster that's after us will tear up the entire forest to find us, if it has to.[lr]::
23679::$$$message_0180_0008_0003$$$::If it catches up to us, our temporary shelter will be as good as gravel.[lr]::
23680::$$$message_0180_0008_0004$$$::It's like trying to fight a storm. A human can't stand up to a natural disaster, no matter what manner of Mystics they possess.[wdash canskip=0]::
23681::$$$message_0180_0009_0000$$$::We encountered the monster in a forest clearing.[lr]::
23682::$$$message_0180_0009_0001$$$::No, it would be more accurate to say he was expecting us.[lr]::
23683::$$$message_0180_0009_0002$$$::Towering over us like a huge stone slab, he roared and attacked as soon as we stepped into his territory.::
23684::$$$message_0180_0010_0000$$$::Our counterattack ended before it even began.[lr]::
23685::$$$message_0180_0010_0001$$$::I never had any desire to fight him, and Bazett understood from the opening shot that there was no battle to fight here.[lr]::
23686::$$$message_0180_0010_0002$$$::She's generally a sore loser when it comes to fighting, but when we faced a monster that Fragarach can't kill, she calmly sounded the retreat.::
23687::$$$message_0180_0011_0000$$$::Still, she tried to stand her ground for a few seconds, as you might expect.[lr]::
23688::$$$message_0180_0011_0001$$$::While I was cowed by the monster's war cry, she immediately fired a shot from Fragarach.::
23689::$$$message_0180_0012_0000$$$::The monster's Noble Phantasm is the kind that's always active, so she was able to unleash Fragarach immediately.[lr]::
23690::$$$message_0180_0012_0001$$$::Fragarach unerringly pierced his heart, and the monster seemed to be dead...until he revived less than ten seconds later and charged at us again.[lr]::
23691::$$$message_0180_0012_0002$$$::He died and came back to life, right on the spot.[lr]::
23692::$$$message_0180_0012_0003$$$::That undying body is probably his Noble Phantasm.::
23693::$$$message_0180_0013_0000$$$::After using Fragarach, Bazett froze.[lr]::
23694::$$$message_0180_0013_0001$$$::I kicked her out of the way, since it didn't look like she was going to avoid that giant's charge.::
23695::$$$message_0180_0014_0000$$$::Ow. It grazed me and sent me flying.[lr]::
23696::$$$message_0180_0014_0001$$$::Missing its charge, the monster changed targets and brought its stone slab of an axe down on me.[lr]::
23697::$$$message_0180_0014_0002$$$::Taking the hit isn't an option. I have to go all-or-nothing and try to evade, and just as I think that I'm as good as dead...[lr]::
23698::$$$message_0180_0014_0003$$$::Bazett recovers from my kick and sends a second Fragarach at the monster's face.::
23699::$$$message_0180_0015_0000$$$::"We're getting out of here! Stay with me!"[lr]::
23700::$$$message_0180_0015_0001$$$::Looks like she used the second Fragarach to blind, rather than kill him.[lr]::
23701::$$$message_0180_0015_0002$$$::While the monster wildly swings its axe with a gaping hole in its head, Bazett grabs my hand and we run into the forest.[lr]::
23702::$$$message_0180_0015_0003$$$::Shedding a glove scorched by Fragarach's launch, she inscribed Runes of swiftness onto her legs.[lr]::
23703::$$$message_0180_0015_0004$$$::As for me, I pick up the discarded trash. What can I say, I have sticky fingers.::
23704::$$$message_0180_0016_0000$$$::"No dawdling! Hurry! We need to get some distance on that thing!"[lr]::
23705::$$$message_0180_0016_0001$$$::Bazett grabs me by the scruff of the neck and starts running.[lr]::
23706::$$$message_0180_0016_0002$$$::Thanks to her already impressive physical strength and the power of the Runes, we're gaining distance from the big guy.[lr]::
23707::$$$message_0180_0016_0003$$$::But our advantage won't last more than a few seconds.[lr]::
23708::$$$message_0180_0016_0004$$$::The monster regenerates its eyes and makes a beeline for us, as if on our scent.::
23709::$$$message_0180_0017_0000$$$::"...And that's how we've gotten this far.[lr]::
23710::$$$message_0180_0017_0001$$$::All signs point to him catching up and killing us in a matter of minutes.[lr]::
23711::$$$message_0180_0017_0002$$$::I told you how dangerous he is, but you just had to try anyway.[lr]::
23712::$$$message_0180_0017_0003$$$::Am I wrong, Master?"[lr]::
23713::$$$message_0180_0017_0004$$$::"I-I admit I underestimated the enemy's strength. I didn't expect a Servant like that."::
23714::$$$message_0180_0018_0000$$$::Bazett's response is slightly tinged with remorse.[lr]::
23715::$$$message_0180_0018_0001$$$::It's a world of difference compared to the total silence since we entered the forest.[lr]::
23716::$$$message_0180_0018_0002$$$::While this is more comfortable for me, first things first[line len=2]::
23717::$$$message_0180_0019_0000$$$::"That's no Servant. It's just a monster that lives in the forest. Think of it as a wraith that failed to become a Servant."[lr]::
23718::$$$message_0180_0019_0001$$$::"What are you talking about? That's a Servant. It's no wraith of the current era. It has a Noble Phantasm, and it's clearly the Einzberns' Servant."::
23719::$$$message_0180_0020_0000$$$::"Hmm... It fits that position, yeah.[lr]::
23720::$$$message_0180_0020_0001$$$::I see, I see. A Servant is a Servant, whether it's our competitor or not."[lr]::
23721::$$$message_0180_0020_0002$$$::There's no point in guessing what its original class might have been.[lr]::
23722::$$$message_0180_0020_0003$$$::What's important now is how we deal with it. No, we already know we can't beat it, but we need to figure out our next move.::
23723::$$$message_0180_0021_0000$$$::"What now, Master?[lr]::
23724::$$$message_0180_0021_0001$$$::Just let it kill us and start over?[lr]::
23725::$$$message_0180_0021_0002$$$::Or do you want to find its Master?"::
23726::$$$message_0180_0022_0000$$$::"We'll find the Einzbern Master, of course. There weren't any signs of her near the Servant, so she must be lurking in the castle."[lr]::
23727::$$$message_0180_0022_0001$$$::"I agree, but how are we gonna get there with the giant still around?[lr]::
23728::$$$message_0180_0022_0002$$$::We can run or fight. What do you intend to do?"::
23729::$$$message_0180_0023_0000$$$::"...Avenger, to be frank, I'm loath to turn my back on an enemy. When I face a challenge, my style is to overcome it with brute force."[lr]::
23730::$$$message_0180_0023_0001$$$::"I know. We've been together long enough. You've always thrown me into losing battles that we win by the skin of our teeth."::
23731::$$$message_0180_0024_0000$$$::"Th-that's because I misunderstood your power as a time loop. If you were a more normal Servant, I wouldn't have to take such desperate measures."[lr]::
23732::$$$message_0180_0024_0001$$$::"You sure about that? Is that what we're going to do this time? Either way, there's no getting to the castle without dealing with the big guy."::
23733::$$$message_0180_0025_0000$$$::"...No. Even I'm not that reckless.[lr]::
23734::$$$message_0180_0025_0001$$$::We've had a fighting chance in all of our battles thus far, but I don't see any way to beat this enemy. It's too poor of a match for us."::
23735::$$$message_0180_0026_0000$$$::I whistle.[lr]::
23736::$$$message_0180_0026_0001$$$::Bazett's right. It's the worst possible matchup.[lr]::
23737::$$$message_0180_0026_0002$$$::I can't use my Noble Phantasm on it.[lr]::
23738::$$$message_0180_0026_0003$$$::All of its attacks are lethal, so I'll die as soon as it hits me. I won't have a chance to return the damage.::
23739::$$$message_0180_0027_0000$$$::Meanwhile, even though Bazett can use Fragarach, she's limited to three uses.[lr]::
23740::$$$message_0180_0027_0001$$$::The monster clearly has the ability to revive itself from death.[lr]::
23741::$$$message_0180_0027_0002$$$::I'm not sure how many times it can revive, but probably more than three.::
23742::$$$message_0180_0028_0000$$$::"So fighting is out. That leaves..."[lr]::
23743::$$$message_0180_0028_0001$$$::"We should retrace our steps and head for the castle. Our chances aren't good, but still better than zero."::
23744::$$$message_0180_0029_0000$$$::That's the right answer.[lr]::
23745::$$$message_0180_0029_0001$$$::Just one pitfall, though: [lr]::
23746::$$$message_0180_0029_0002$$$::We can't ignore that monster.[lr]::
23747::$$$message_0180_0029_0003$$$::Bazett needs to deal with it somehow if she wants to reach the castle.::
23748::$$$message_0180_0030_0000$$$::"That settles it. I'll stay here and draw the monster off, while you go to the castle alone.[lr]::
23749::$$$message_0180_0030_0001$$$::Okay, that gives us a 50/50 chance. As long as you don't get turned around, you'll definitely make it to the castle with those legs.[lr]::
23750::$$$message_0180_0030_0002$$$::The castle is about fifteen kilometers to the northwest.[lr]::
23751::$$$message_0180_0030_0003$$$::Do you still have your Rune-carving claws? You do. Then this should work. I can only buy you about a minute, but you're more than capable of making good speed without me."::
23752::$$$message_0180_0031_0000$$$::"...Avenger, I never ordered you to do that. We're going to the castle together."[lr]::
23753::$$$message_0180_0031_0001$$$::"Don't be crazy. That's actually harder for me.[lr]::
23754::$$$message_0180_0031_0002$$$::If I'm being straight with you, I can't even keep up. It took everything I had just to run this far. If you have to slow down for me, it'll definitely catch up to you."::
23755::$$$message_0180_0032_0000$$$::"That's only because your spirit is weak.[lr]::
23756::$$$message_0180_0032_0001$$$::Pull yourself together. You should be able to run if you really want to. You always give up too early."[lr]::
23757::$$$message_0180_0032_0002$$$::"Nnn..."[lr]::
23758::$$$message_0180_0032_0003$$$::That struck a nerve.[lr]::
23759::$$$message_0180_0032_0004$$$::Bazett's the kind of person to tough anything out until the very end.::
23760::$$$message_0180_0033_0000$$$::"Okay, fine, I can still work if I kick my ass into gear.[lr]::
23761::$$$message_0180_0033_0001$$$::But I honestly can't keep up with your speed."[lr]::
23762::$$$message_0180_0033_0002$$$::"...Good grief. Then stop thinking of it in fighting terms. Just turn into spirit form if you have to."::
23763::$$$message_0180_0034_0000$$$::A very rational opinion, but it doesn't help either of us.[lr]::
23764::$$$message_0180_0034_0001$$$::What to do...?[lr]::
23765::$$$message_0180_0034_0002$$$::Our respective roles are usually so much simpler.[lr]::
23766::$$$message_0180_0034_0003$$$::Now she's making silly misunderstandings because we're out of our element.::
23767::$$$message_0180_0035_0000$$$::"...Haah. This isn't like you, Master. What would be the point of me going into my spirit form and protecting only myself? If you die, then so do I. You should act more like a commander and cut your dead weight to finish the mission."[lr]::
23768::$$$message_0180_0035_0001$$$::"...I've never once called or thought of you as dead weight."::
23769::$$$message_0180_0036_0000$$$::"But I do. Anyway, I'm gonna slow you down."[lr]::
23770::$$$message_0180_0036_0001$$$::To prove the point, I stick out my left foot.[lr]::
23771::$$$message_0180_0036_0002$$$::One of my legs got crippled by the monster's charge.[lr]::
23772::$$$message_0180_0036_0003$$$::I only made it this far because I was trying to show off how amazing a Heroic Spirit is, even if I'm the absolute bottom of the barrel.[lr]::
23773::$$$message_0180_0036_0004$$$::Mm, guess I can't make fun of her now.::
23774::$$$message_0180_0037_0000$$$::"No. Then I'm staying with you. We'll find a way to beat the Servant here.[lr]::
23775::$$$message_0180_0037_0001$$$::I'm not going on alone. I... I can't leave you behind."::
23776::$$$message_0180_0038_0000$$$::Uncertain determination.[lr]::
23777::$$$message_0180_0038_0001$$$::I'm sure it isn't out of any affection.[lr]::
23778::$$$message_0180_0038_0002$$$::It's just the usual hopeless misunderstandings she's making.::
23779::$$$message_0180_0039_0000$$$::"...Because you pity me?"[lr]::
23780::$$$message_0180_0039_0001$$$::"N-no. This isn't pity.[lr]::
23781::$$$message_0180_0039_0002$$$::You got injured because of me, so I can at least take responsibility for it..."::
23782::$$$message_0180_0040_0000$$$::"That's backwards.[lr]::
23783::$$$message_0180_0040_0001$$$::Master, you just said that you want to stay not to achieve your goal, but to help me.[lr]::
23784::$$$message_0180_0040_0002$$$::And yeah, that ain't so bad. I want you to help me, if you can.[lr]::
23785::$$$message_0180_0040_0003$$$::But if you feel obliged to me, then that's even worse than leaving me behind."[lr]::
23786::$$$message_0180_0040_0004$$$::"Obliged...?"::
23787::$$$message_0180_0041_0000$$$::"Yeah. That's what feelings like pity and mercy are.[lr]::
23788::$$$message_0180_0041_0001$$$::Listen, young human girl. If you want to save someone from despair, you shouldn't do it out of pity."::
23789::$$$message_0180_0042_0000$$$::"Only the positive can cancel out the negative. Trying to scoop someone out of their grief with your own sadness won't heal them at all.[lr]::
23790::$$$message_0180_0042_0001$$$::...I guess it's a different story if you've got society to give them some TLC afterward. Very few people have that much free time, though.[lr]::
23791::$$$message_0180_0042_0002$$$::If you're going to save someone, then you need to gain something from it. Otherwise, it's a lose-lose."::
23792::$$$message_0180_0043_0000$$$::I snicker.[lr]::
23793::$$$message_0180_0043_0001$$$::The monster roars in the distance.[lr]::
23794::$$$message_0180_0043_0002$$$::Bazett stares at me blankly.::
23795::$$$message_0180_0044_0000$$$::"Was that hard to understand? Then let me use an allegory.[lr]::
23796::$$$message_0180_0044_0001$$$::Let's say that somewhere, there exists the unluckiest guy in the world. One day, you learn of him and feel sad. That's a pointless sentiment.[lr]::
23797::$$$message_0180_0044_0002$$$::You can't get involved with something on the other side of the world. Even if someone is having awful luck in a place that has nothing to do with you, you should laugh."::
23798::$$$message_0180_0045_0000$$$::...Yeah. Trying to save someone who doesn't even exist in your world is like denying your whole world.[lr]::
23799::$$$message_0180_0045_0001$$$::It's an unspoken law of existence.[lr]::
23800::$$$message_0180_0045_0002$$$::People who have nothing to do with each other, who have no quarrel with  anyone, affirm of all kinds of misfortune just by existing.[lr]::
23801::$$$message_0180_0045_0003$$$::There's no denying that inequality. How could you go on if you couldn't accept the fact that your own good fortune has to come at someone else's expense?::
23802::$$$message_0180_0046_0000$$$::You should laugh and accept your own blessed life, even if someone else has to live a wretched one. Otherwise, it would all be a mistake.[lr]::
23803::$$$message_0180_0046_0001$$$::To face that ugly contradiction for the rest of your life is what it means to be a proper human being.::
23804::$$$message_0180_0047_0000$$$::Humans can only save themselves.[lr]::
23805::$$$message_0180_0047_0001$$$::Claiming to save others for their sake is an excuse worthy of death.[lr]::
23806::$$$message_0180_0047_0002$$$::Those pretty words can't save anyone.[lr]::
23807::$$$message_0180_0047_0003$$$::But... If one still believes one can save somebody else...[lr]::
23808::$$$message_0180_0047_0004$$$::If you want to save somebody else...::
23809::$$$message_0180_0048_0000$$$::"...I know; if you want to help, at least laugh while you save that luckless guy.[lr]::
23810::$$$message_0180_0048_0001$$$::Whether you stay because you can't abandon me or come back because you feel sorry for me, nobody asked you to do that. No matter what, don't think about sticking together through thick and thin."::
23811::$$$message_0180_0049_0000$$$::All we need to share is pleasure.[lr]::
23812::$$$message_0180_0049_0001$$$::It would just bother me if she came back for me because of anguish.[lr]::
23813::$$$message_0180_0049_0002$$$::What I want is an unconditional happy ending.[lr]::
23814::$$$message_0180_0049_0003$$$::Love and peace that overrides all the lost days.[lr]::
23815::$$$message_0180_0049_0004$$$::...Yeah.[lr]::
23816::$$$message_0180_0049_0005$$$::I want you to use a helping hand...[lr]::
23817::$$$message_0180_0049_0006$$$::...to help these dark, sunken eyes see a brighter future.::
23818::$$$message_0180_0050_0000$$$::"Avenger, you..."[lr]::
23819::$$$message_0180_0050_0001$$$::"Ah, I got off topic.[lr]::
23820::$$$message_0180_0050_0002$$$::To sum it up, just get going. I'll see you again even if I die, so it's awkward that you're feeling sorry for me.[lr]::
23821::$$$message_0180_0050_0003$$$::You still need to talk to the Einzbern Master, remember? Go take care of business.[wvl][se volume=60 storage=se158.wav] I'll just be heading back ahead of you."::
23822::$$$message_0180_0051_0000$$$::...A storm approaches.[lr]::
23823::$$$message_0180_0051_0001$$$::We'd better cut the chatter.::
23824::$$$message_0180_0052_0000$$$::"What, you need me to say something else?"[lr]::
23825::$$$message_0180_0052_0001$$$::"...No. That was enough.[lr]::
23826::$$$message_0180_0052_0002$$$::Please slow the enemy down for me, Avenger."[lr]::
23827::$$$message_0180_0052_0003$$$::"Sure thing. Well, guess I'd better go man up and meet him. Go take the back way out."::
23828::$$$message_0180_0053_0000$$$::I wave at Bazett and go outside.[lr]::
23829::$$$message_0180_0053_0001$$$::She doesn't waste time once she's made up her mind. By now, she should be on her way to the castle at full speed.::
23830::$$$message_0180_0054_0000$$$::The Einzberns' Servant should be here any moment.[lr]::
23831::$$$message_0180_0054_0001$$$::I put Bazett's discarded glove on my right hand.[lr]::
23832::$$$message_0180_0054_0002$$$::It got burned mostly to cinders when she used Fragarach, but I'll treat it like a lucky charm.::
23833::$$$message_0180_0055_0000$$$::"...I wonder if he'll cut me clean in two this time.[lr]::
23834::$$$message_0180_0055_0001$$$::Shit, that's why I said I didn't want to come here."[lr]::
23835::$$$message_0180_0055_0002$$$::The strongest attacking the weakest.[lr]::
23836::$$$message_0180_0055_0003$$$::Jeez, there's way too many of these lopsided matchups in the Holy Grail War.::
23837::$$$message_0180_0056_0000$$$::And then I left him.[lr]::
23838::$$$message_0180_0056_0001$$$::I run through the forest alone, knowing that he's guaranteed to die.::
23839::$$$message_0180_0057_0000$$$::I don't feel indebted to him.[lr]::
23840::$$$message_0180_0057_0001$$$::As he said, this was the obvious choice.[lr]::
23841::$$$message_0180_0057_0002$$$::A familiar is an expendable pawn meant to protect its master. It makes perfect sense to use my Servant as a shield to survive.[lr]::
23842::$$$message_0180_0057_0003$$$::I'll only feel guilt if I can't reach the castle.[lr]::
23843::$$$message_0180_0057_0004$$$::I'll probably feel that way the moment I fail to answer his sacrifice with success.::
23844::$$$message_0180_0058_0000$$$::"...Ngh."[lr]::
23845::$$$message_0180_0058_0001$$$::I'm used to it, and I understand it.[lr]::
23846::$$$message_0180_0058_0002$$$::Avenger will resurrect if he dies, anyway.[lr]::
23847::$$$message_0180_0058_0003$$$::It just means that he'll return to the first night before I do.[lr]::
23848::$$$message_0180_0058_0004$$$::I won't lose anything.[lr]::
23849::$$$message_0180_0058_0005$$$::There's nothing to regret.[lr]::
23850::$$$message_0180_0058_0006$$$::I just need to take the best course of action like I always have, befitting my name and status as a mage of the Association.::
23851::$$$message_0180_0059_0000$$$::And yet, it hurts.[lr]::
23852::$$$message_0180_0059_0001$$$::I gnash my teeth at the sentimentality gnawing at my chest.[lr]::
23853::$$$message_0180_0059_0002$$$::My frustration at both him and myself makes me want to destroy everything I see.::
23854::$$$message_0180_0060_0000$$$::The darkness of the night, the abundant trees, and the castle beyond them[line len=2]if I could afford to, I'd break them all to bits.[lr]::
23855::$$$message_0180_0060_0001$$$::But the thing I want to destroy the most right now isn't those voiceless things, but rather...[lr]::
23856::$$$message_0180_0060_0002$$$::"Oh. So I too..."::
23857::$$$message_0180_0061_0000$$$::                                                    I left him behind.::
23858::$$$message_0180_0062_0000$$$::Suddenly, I want to apologize to everything I've never known.[lr]::
23859::$$$message_0180_0062_0001$$$::Even if it was the obvious choice. Even if he suggested it to me.[lr]::
23860::$$$message_0180_0062_0002$$$::Even if it's a feeling worse than hatred or treachery...::
23861::$$$message_0180_0063_0000$$$::The castle gate is open.[lr]::
23862::$$$message_0180_0063_0001$$$::I hurry past it without stopping.[lr]::
23863::$$$message_0180_0063_0002$$$::The monster is far behind me, but I probably have less than five minutes.[lr]::
23864::$$$message_0180_0063_0003$$$::Before that, I need to find the Einzbern Master and make them submit.::
23865::$$$message_0180_0064_0000$$$::...I need to stay calm.[lr]::
23866::$$$message_0180_0064_0001$$$::My goal isn't to eliminate the other Master, but to have my questions answered.[lr]::
23867::$$$message_0180_0064_0002$$$::The Einzbern Master, the lynchpin of the Holy Grail War, knows more about Heroic Spirits than anyone else. I need their help to solve the mystery of these four days.::
23868::$$$message_0180_0065_0000$$$::I kick the front door open and rush inside.[lr]::
23869::$$$message_0180_0065_0001$$$::No point in stealth. They should be aware of me ever since I engaged the monster.[lr]::
23870::$$$message_0180_0065_0002$$$::"...They're close. Forward, on the second floor!"::
23871::$$$message_0180_0066_0000$$$::I run toward the stairs and put on a fresh pair of gloves.[lr]::
23872::$$$message_0180_0066_0001$$$::This is the heart of the enemy camp. An attack could come at any moment[line len=2][lr]::
23873::$$$message_0180_0066_0002$$$::"Fuh...!"[lr]::
23874::$$$message_0180_0066_0003$$$::Attacks come from every direction!::
23875::$$$message_0180_0067_0000$$$::An anachronistic polearm swings at me.[lr]::
23876::$$$message_0180_0067_0001$$$::It's a halberd.[fg textoff=0 left=270 opacity=0 index=1000 top=10 time=100 storage=リズハルバード01a(中)][lr]::
23877::$$$message_0180_0067_0002$$$::Such weapons have gone out of fashion even with the Holy Church's knights. I evade, jumping backward.[wt canskip=0][wm canskip=0][current withback=false]::
23878::$$$message_0180_0068_0000$$$::"...Intruder. If you're here to bully Illya, then leave."[lr]::
23879::$$$message_0180_0068_0001$$$::Her voice is emotionless.[lr]::
23880::$$$message_0180_0068_0002$$$::She easily wields a weapon that has to be over forty kilograms[line len=2]no, her movements are clumsy, but it's like she doesn't feel the weight.[lr]::
23881::$$$message_0180_0068_0003$$$::There's no doubt that this is an Einzbern homunculus designed for combat...!::
23882::$$$message_0180_0069_0000$$$::"...You won't leave? Then too bad."[lr]::
23883::$$$message_0180_0069_0001$$$::Sensing my hostility, the homunculus raises her halberd.[lr]::
23884::$$$message_0180_0069_0002$$$::There's no time to gauge her strength.[lr]::
23885::$$$message_0180_0069_0003$$$::I charge in to finish this with a full-power strike from the get-go.[lr]::
23886::$$$message_0180_0069_0004$$$::This is my second time fighting an Einzbern homunculus, so I know how dangerous they are. But I also know their limits...!::
23887::$$$message_0180_0070_0000$$$::"Rrgh...!"[lr]::
23888::$$$message_0180_0070_0001$$$::I step back and create some distance after several exchanges of attack and defense.[lr]::
23889::$$$message_0180_0070_0002$$$::Her movements are childish, relying on her inhuman strength.[lr]::
23890::$$$message_0180_0070_0003$$$::Still, it's like fighting a bladed gale.[lr]::
23891::$$$message_0180_0070_0004$$$::She doesn't measure up to the monster I ran from, but this homunculus is lethal enough.[lr]::
23892::$$$message_0180_0070_0005$$$::Taking a single hit would be enough to crush my bones.::
23893::$$$message_0180_0071_0000$$$::I threw seven punches while evading her halberd.[lr]::
23894::$$$message_0180_0071_0001$$$::Each of them connected solidly enough to punch someone's organs out of their torso, but the homunculus didn't seem to react.[lr]::
23895::$$$message_0180_0071_0002$$$::Either her maid uniform is a superbly-crafted Mystic Code, or she just doesn't feel pain.[lr]::
23896::$$$message_0180_0071_0003$$$::Either way, I'll have to immobilize her by breaking her bones[line len=2]::
23897::$$$message_0180_0072_0000$$$::"...Ah."[lr]::
23898::$$$message_0180_0072_0001$$$::...?[lr]::
23899::$$$message_0180_0072_0002$$$::The homunculus lowers her guard.[lr]::
23900::$$$message_0180_0072_0003$$$::The will to fight suddenly drains from her impassive vigor.::
23901::$$$message_0180_0073_0000$$$::"That's enough, Leys.[lr]::
23902::$$$message_0180_0073_0001$$$::She's my guest. I told you to be polite, remember?"::
23903::$$$message_0180_0074_0000$$$::A girl with hair as white as snow stands at the top of the stairs.::
23904::$$$message_0180_0075_0000$$$::"Good evening, unfamiliar guest.[lr]::
23905::$$$message_0180_0075_0001$$$::I'm Illyasviel von Einzbern, the lord of this castle. What business have you here this night?"[lr]::
23906::$$$message_0180_0075_0002$$$::The girl greets me with adorable decorum to match her lovely appearance.::
23907::$$$message_0180_0076_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23908::$$$message_0180_0076_0001$$$::This girl is the Einzberns' Master...?[lr]::
23909::$$$message_0180_0076_0002$$$::I can feel powerful magical energy from her. It's an outrageous amount, actually.[lr]::
23910::$$$message_0180_0076_0003$$$::She must have been born to be a superhuman container of Magic Circuits.[lr]::
23911::$$$message_0180_0076_0004$$$::There's no doubt about it.[lr]::
23912::$$$message_0180_0076_0005$$$::This girl is another Einzbern homunculus.::
23913::$$$message_0180_0077_0000$$$::"Oh. No greeting, after I came all this way?[lr]::
23914::$$$message_0180_0077_0001$$$::It seems the mages that work for the Mage's Association aren't very polite. If you aren't here to talk, then please leave."::
23915::$$$message_0180_0078_0000$$$::She giggles.[lr]::
23916::$$$message_0180_0078_0001$$$::She knows I'm a Master, but she isn't cautious of me at all.[lr]::
23917::$$$message_0180_0078_0002$$$::It's as if...[lr]::
23918::$$$message_0180_0078_0003$$$::...she doesn't see me as a threat.::
23919::$$$message_0180_0079_0000$$$::"...Pardon me. I'm Bazett. The Mage's Association sent me. I'm also here as a Master."::
23920::$$$message_0180_0080_0000$$$::"I know this. You met my Servant in the forest, right?[lr]::
23921::$$$message_0180_0080_0001$$$::I was wondering if you'd show up here.[lr]::
23922::$$$message_0180_0080_0002$$$::The other Masters avoid this place, no matter what. I was happy when I saw that you came."::
23923::$$$message_0180_0081_0000$$$::"...Huh?"[lr]::
23924::$$$message_0180_0081_0001$$$::She's wearing a carefree smile.[lr]::
23925::$$$message_0180_0081_0002$$$::...My first impression might have been off.[lr]::
23926::$$$message_0180_0081_0003$$$::It's not that she's underestimated me; maybe she genuinely doesn't see me as an enemy.::
23927::$$$message_0180_0082_0000$$$::"Hehe. That's right. I don't want to fight you.[lr]::
23928::$$$message_0180_0082_0001$$$::Actually, I don't want to fight the other Masters, either. I'm not a Master anymore, after all.[lr]::
23929::$$$message_0180_0082_0002$$$::All the other Masters know this. That's why they don't come to the forest."[lr]::
23930::$$$message_0180_0082_0003$$$::"Wha..."[lr]::
23931::$$$message_0180_0082_0004$$$::She's not a Master...?[lr]::
23932::$$$message_0180_0082_0005$$$::What's the meaning of[line len=2]::
23933::$$$message_0180_0083_0000$$$::"You're dismissed, Leys. I want to talk to Bazett. Go close the front gate so that the forest ghosts don't get in here."[lr]::
23934::$$$message_0180_0083_0001$$$::"...Okay. Illya will really be fine...?"[lr]::
23935::$$$message_0180_0083_0002$$$::"Yeah. I want to talk to Bazett in private.[lr]::
23936::$$$message_0180_0083_0003$$$::Leys, you've been a little cheeky lately. Stop talking back."[lr]::
23937::$$$message_0180_0083_0004$$$::"...Mm-hmm. I'll do what you say, Illya."::
23938::$$$message_0180_0084_0000$$$::The homunculus she calls "Leys" walks breezily by me, as if we hadn't been trying to kill each other moments ago.::
23939::$$$message_0180_0085_0000$$$::"Over here, Bazett.[lr]::
23940::$$$message_0180_0085_0001$$$::You came to talk, right? I'll tell you what I know."[lr]::
23941::$$$message_0180_0085_0002$$$::The girl comes down the stairs and disappears into the back of the lobby.[lr]::
23942::$$$message_0180_0085_0003$$$::"..."[lr]::
23943::$$$message_0180_0085_0004$$$::Puzzled by this unexpected development, I accept the girl's invitation.::
23944::$$$message_0180_0086_0000$$$::"I believe I have a good grasp of the situation.[lr]::
23945::$$$message_0180_0086_0001$$$::You entered my forest, got attacked by a ghost, and then used your Servant as a decoy so you could get here.[lr]::
23946::$$$message_0180_0086_0002$$$::Your goal is to defeat the Einzbern Master and learn some information.[lr]::
23947::$$$message_0180_0086_0003$$$::Am I wrong? I don't think you would have gone to all this trouble otherwise."::
23948::$$$message_0180_0087_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23949::$$$message_0180_0087_0001$$$::The girl settles comfortably into her chair, while I decline to sit.[lr]::
23950::$$$message_0180_0087_0002$$$::This is still enemy territory, even if she doesn't want to fight right now.[lr]::
23951::$$$message_0180_0087_0003$$$::All it would take is a flick of her finger to erase this room and everything in it.::
23952::$$$message_0180_0088_0000$$$::"You're cautious, Bazett. I wonder if the Association taught you that, or if it's just your personality.[lr]::
23953::$$$message_0180_0088_0001$$$::Are you the type to not accept even a cup of tea offered by an enemy?"[lr]::
23954::$$$message_0180_0088_0002$$$::"...It depends, but I won't partake today.[lr]::
23955::$$$message_0180_0088_0003$$$::As you said, I came here seeking information, not to have a social chat."::
23956::$$$message_0180_0089_0000$$$::"Really? Too bad. I'll call off the tea party, then. You probably just want to stick to business."[lr]::
23957::$$$message_0180_0089_0001$$$::"..."[lr]::
23958::$$$message_0180_0089_0002$$$::I'm starting to doubt that this girl is really the Einzbern Master.[lr]::
23959::$$$message_0180_0089_0003$$$::No, if what she said about no longer being a Master is true, then she really isn't.::
23960::$$$message_0180_0090_0000$$$::"...Illyasviel.[lr]::
23961::$$$message_0180_0090_0001$$$::You said that you're not a Master. So is the giant in the forest not your Servant?"[lr]::
23962::$$$message_0180_0090_0002$$$::"That ghost is my Servant, but not the Einzberns' Servant. I made a small blunder and it went crazy.[lr]::
23963::$$$message_0180_0090_0003$$$::Now it's just a ghost that cares only about protecting me, not winning the Holy Grail War."::
23964::$$$message_0180_0091_0000$$$::"It's...different from the monsters appearing in town, but you can think of them as the same thing.[lr]::
23965::$$$message_0180_0091_0001$$$::He has nothing to do with the Holy Grail War. He's just a monster that kills Masters who enter this forest. A shapeless wraith who is a Servant, but could not attain a purpose befitting a Servant."::
23966::$$$message_0180_0092_0000$$$::"He couldn't attain a purpose...?"[lr]::
23967::$$$message_0180_0092_0001$$$::"Yes. I didn't give him a fitting job, so he never had a chance to do his duty.[lr]::
23968::$$$message_0180_0092_0002$$$::If he had been a Servant of the Einzberns, that never would have happened."::
23969::$$$message_0180_0093_0000$$$::"...You're saying that isn't the Einzberns' Servant? Then where is the Einzberns' Servant?"::
23970::$$$message_0180_0094_0000$$$::"Gone.[lr]::
23971::$$$message_0180_0094_0001$$$::Another Master took my Servant from me."::
23972::$$$message_0180_0095_0000$$$::"That's why I said I'm no longer a Master.[lr]::
23973::$$$message_0180_0095_0001$$$::Four days after the Holy Grail War started, the Einzbern Master's Servant was killed, and she failed.[lr]::
23974::$$$message_0180_0095_0002$$$::Your Servant should have known all along that the Einzberns already dropped out of the war."::
23975::$$$message_0180_0096_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23976::$$$message_0180_0096_0001$$$::My mind freezes.[lr]::
23977::$$$message_0180_0096_0002$$$::Avenger knew that the Einzbern Master already forfeited.[lr]::
23978::$$$message_0180_0096_0003$$$::...That's fine.[lr]::
23979::$$$message_0180_0096_0004$$$::He's been hiding so much from me and I don't trust him, so it's not a shock to hear that.[lr]::
23980::$$$message_0180_0096_0005$$$::More importantly...::
23981::$$$message_0180_0097_0000$$$::"What's wrong? Did something I said bother you?"[lr]::
23982::$$$message_0180_0097_0001$$$::She giggles.[lr]::
23983::$$$message_0180_0097_0002$$$::This girl already knows everything.::
23984::$$$message_0180_0098_0000$$$::"Illyasviel.[lr]::
23985::$$$message_0180_0098_0001$$$::When you say another Master took your Servant, you mean..."[lr]::
23986::$$$message_0180_0098_0002$$$::"Oh, didn't you know?[lr]::
23987::$$$message_0180_0098_0003$$$::His name is Avenger. The oldest malice bearing the title Aŋra Mainiiu.::
23988::$$$message_0180_0099_0000$$$::There's something like a crack as my consciousness distorts.[lr]::
23989::$$$message_0180_0099_0001$$$::I find myself gripping the earring in my pocket.[lr]::
23990::$$$message_0180_0099_0002$$$::I try to get my breath under control.[lr]::
23991::$$$message_0180_0099_0003$$$::"That...doesn't make sense.[lr]::
23992::$$$message_0180_0099_0004$$$::I've never heard of a class called Avenger.[lr]::
23993::$$$message_0180_0099_0005$$$::There shouldn't even be a Heroic Spirit named Aŋra Mainiiu."[lr]::
23994::$$$message_0180_0099_0006$$$::I voice the doubt I've had all along.::
23995::$$$message_0180_0100_0000$$$::"Yes, of course, Aŋra Mainiiu itself doesn't exist. The thing summoned as Avenger is just a person who falsely claimed that name.[lr]::
23996::$$$message_0180_0100_0001$$$::He's a normal person who knows nothing about magecraft or Mystics, and has nothing to do with mythological evils.[lr]::
23997::$$$message_0180_0100_0002$$$::He was just a human sacrifice, chosen to be an icon and reviled as a devil all his life."::
23998::$$$message_0180_0101_0000$$$::It's a tale from a distant world.[lr]::
23999::$$$message_0180_0101_0001$$$::There was once a community who shunned worldly conflict and built a secluded world in the mountains.[lr]::
24000::$$$message_0180_0101_0002$$$::They gathered to embody human goodness, but they couldn't rid themselves of evil.::
24001::$$$message_0180_0102_0000$$$::Doubt. Deception. Hatred. Resentment.[lr]::
24002::$$$message_0180_0102_0001$$$::The more they venerated goodness, the more they created evil.[lr]::
24003::$$$message_0180_0102_0002$$$::They tried to solve this by assigning that ugliness to a specific person.[lr]::
24004::$$$message_0180_0102_0003$$$::Evil isn't born from within.[lr]::
24005::$$$message_0180_0102_0004$$$::Their evil can't have been real.[lr]::
24006::$$$message_0180_0102_0005$$$::Human evil was a poison inflicted by a devil. They had to correct this and purify themselves.[lr]::
24007::$$$message_0180_0102_0006$$$::So...::
24008::$$$message_0180_0103_0000$$$::They needed a root of all evil.[lr]::
24009::$$$message_0180_0103_0001$$$::They needed an icon that embodied all sin.[lr]::
24010::$$$message_0180_0103_0002$$$::Someone to point the finger and say, "only you are evil."[lr]::
24011::$$$message_0180_0103_0003$$$::They made a human sacrifice who would represent all the evil in the world.::
24012::$$$message_0180_0104_0000$$$::"There are some beings like that among the Heroic Spirits.[lr]::
24013::$$$message_0180_0104_0001$$$::They might have lived a normal life, but after they died, they get deified and made into heroes.[lr]::
24014::$$$message_0180_0104_0002$$$::The dead tell no tales, so they can't protest against a convenient role being forced onto their name. They become a target of worship by unthinking, good people."::
24015::$$$message_0180_0105_0000$$$::"...But it was excessive, in his case.[lr]::
24016::$$$message_0180_0105_0001$$$::I wonder if it's because their 'worship' was rage and hatred.[lr]::
24017::$$$message_0180_0105_0002$$$::They treated him as an actual devil and blamed him for everything.[lr]::
24018::$$$message_0180_0105_0003$$$::They feared poverty, disease, disaster, even death itself, believing that these all existed because he did, and blamed him for all of it."::
24019::$$$message_0180_0106_0000$$$::"But it saved them.[lr]::
24020::$$$message_0180_0106_0001$$$::They could accept that evil existed because a devil caused it. It can't have come from them, because it came from him.[lr]::
24021::$$$message_0180_0106_0002$$$::That's why he was treated like a Heroic Spirit after he died.[lr]::
24022::$$$message_0180_0106_0003$$$::Nobody revered him and he didn't do anything to earn it, but he still ended up saving the people."::
24023::$$$message_0180_0107_0000$$$::He became a god while he lived.[lr]::
24024::$$$message_0180_0107_0001$$$::Had his humanity stripped away while he lived.[lr]::
24025::$$$message_0180_0107_0002$$$::Had his birth name taken from him, just so he could be labeled as evil.::
24026::$$$message_0180_0108_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"My name is [font italic=false]gone[font italic=true]."[font italic=false][lr]::
24027::$$$message_0180_0108_0001$$$::He said it like it was no big deal.[lr]::
24028::$$$message_0180_0108_0002$$$::[font italic=true]"You can tell me to remember, but that information..."[font italic=false][lr]::
24029::$$$message_0180_0108_0003$$$::"...doesn't exist anywhere in the world," he said without a hint of resentment.[lr]::
24030::$$$message_0180_0108_0004$$$::And to that...[wm canskip=0]::
24031::$$$message_0180_0109_0000$$$::   [font italic=true]"You've grown attached to the name people called you as a hero.[font italic=false][lr]::
24032::$$$message_0180_0109_0001$$$::[font italic=true]It may only be a title, but it was an accolade given by the people. It makes sense you'd like it."[font italic=false][lr]::
24033::$$$message_0180_0109_0002$$$::...How could I have remarked something like that?::
24034::$$$message_0180_0110_0000$$$::"...So that's Avenger.[lr]::
24035::$$$message_0180_0110_0001$$$::A human chosen to represent the evil of Aŋra Mainiiu."[wm canskip=0]::
24036::$$$message_0180_0111_0000$$$::"Yeah. He doesn't have the power to live up to it at all, though.[lr]::
24037::$$$message_0180_0111_0001$$$::They treated him as Aŋra Mainiiu, but faith alone didn't grant him any special powers."::
24038::$$$message_0180_0112_0000$$$::"He was a normal person both before and after he died.[lr]::
24039::$$$message_0180_0112_0001$$$::Mm, since his name got left out of the [font italic=true]Avesta,[font italic=false] he's free from that, at least. But he's too weak to be called a Heroic Spirit.[lr]::
24040::$$$message_0180_0112_0002$$$::Just useless trash by the standards set by the other Servants."[lr]::
24041::$$$message_0180_0112_0003$$$::"Trash...?"::
24042::$$$message_0180_0113_0000$$$::"Hm? What, you wanna fight now? There's nothing to be gained from killing me.[lr]::
24043::$$$message_0180_0113_0001$$$::Anyone ever tell you you're scarier than you look?"::
24044::$$$message_0180_0114_0000$$$::I realize I've taken on an aggressive stance.[lr]::
24045::$$$message_0180_0114_0001$$$::...The girl isn't wrong.[lr]::
24046::$$$message_0180_0114_0002$$$::He is too weak to be a Heroic Spirit, and at first, I thought he was useless, too.[lr]::
24047::$$$message_0180_0114_0003$$$::But that's only because I wasn't perceptive enough to recognize his strengths, which aren't easy to understand.::
24048::$$$message_0180_0115_0000$$$::"No, Bazett. He really was useless in my case.[lr]::
24049::$$$message_0180_0115_0001$$$::It was later that he became the 'hero' that his people wished for. He was as powerless as the day they first made that wish on him. He couldn't even use a Noble Phantasm."::
24050::$$$message_0180_0116_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
24051::$$$message_0180_0116_0001$$$::He couldn't use his Noble Phantasm...?[lr]::
24052::$$$message_0180_0116_0002$$$::Is she saying that Avenger couldn't use his Noble Phantasm when he was still the Einzberns' Servant?::
24053::$$$message_0180_0117_0000$$$::...Something doesn't add up.[lr]::
24054::$$$message_0180_0117_0001$$$::The Einzberns lost their Servant.[lr]::
24055::$$$message_0180_0117_0002$$$::If someone took it, that would have to be me.[lr]::
24056::$$$message_0180_0117_0003$$$::I'm sure that much is true.[lr]::
24057::$$$message_0180_0117_0004$$$::I don't know how it happened, but Avenger's contract was somehow switched from Illyasviel to me.::
24058::$$$message_0180_0118_0000$$$::But what about his death on the fourth day?[lr]::
24059::$$$message_0180_0118_0001$$$::Death is different from losing her Servant.[lr]::
24060::$$$message_0180_0118_0002$$$::She's talking about two different outcomes at the same time.::
24061::$$$message_0180_0119_0000$$$::"Are we done talking about a Servant I don't have anymore?[lr]::
24062::$$$message_0180_0119_0001$$$::I want to ask about your Servant, Bazett. The Mage's Association chose you, so you must have summoned a rather famous one."::
24063::$$$message_0180_0120_0000$$$::"Ah... No, my Servant is..."[lr]::
24064::$$$message_0180_0120_0001$$$::I hesitate before saying it's Avenger.[lr]::
24065::$$$message_0180_0120_0002$$$::I took her Servant, but I feel like there's a lie in here somewhere.::
24066::$$$message_0180_0121_0000$$$::"Your Servant is...?"[lr]::
24067::$$$message_0180_0121_0001$$$::"...You're not a Master anymore, so I don't have to tell you. Besides, he's..."::
24068::$$$message_0180_0122_0000$$$::He's already dead.[lr]::
24069::$$$message_0180_0122_0001$$$::I lost the connection to Avenger when I arrived at this castle.[lr]::
24070::$$$message_0180_0122_0002$$$::He's returned to the first night ahead of me, and he's waiting for me to wake up right now.::
24071::$$$message_0180_0123_0000$$$::"...Yeah. That's his power."[lr]::
24072::$$$message_0180_0123_0001$$$::To revive after death.[lr]::
24073::$$$message_0180_0123_0002$$$::No, to restart from the first day, while we were still alive.[lr]::
24074::$$$message_0180_0123_0003$$$::Doesn't that mean this girl knows we've been going back in time?::
24075::$$$message_0180_0124_0000$$$::"Illyasviel. You said Avenger couldn't use his Noble Phantasm. Which one are you talking about? Avesta, or..."[lr]::
24076::$$$message_0180_0124_0001$$$::"I don't know what you mean, but neither. I told you that Avenger was just a useless tool."::
24077::$$$message_0180_0125_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
24078::$$$message_0180_0125_0001$$$::...That would mean the Einzbern Master doesn't know anything about Avenger's Noble Phantasm.[lr]::
24079::$$$message_0180_0125_0002$$$::Putting Avesta aside, the ability to resurrect from death is outstanding even for a Noble Phantasm.[lr]::
24080::$$$message_0180_0125_0003$$$::No one would ever say it was useless after experiencing it once.::
24081::$$$message_0180_0126_0000$$$::"...I see. We don't need to discuss Avenger, then.[lr]::
24082::$$$message_0180_0126_0001$$$::I'll get to the point, Illyasviel. [cacheimage storage=イリヤ01a(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=イリヤ01a(中)]What is this Holy Grail War like, to you?"[lr]::
24083::$$$message_0180_0126_0002$$$::"That's hard to answer. I'm not part of it anymore, and I'm not interested in it. It's long over, so I'm just taking in the sights."::
24084::$$$message_0180_0127_0000$$$::"You don't know anything about the familiars appearing in town?"[lr]::
24085::$$$message_0180_0127_0001$$$::"Nope. I told you, I'm not part of this.[lr]::
24086::$$$message_0180_0127_0002$$$::But...they won't keep showing up after tonight. They can only exist from the first day until the fourth day."::
24087::$$$message_0180_0128_0000$$$::The four-day limit again.[lr]::
24088::$$$message_0180_0128_0001$$$::I came here to unravel that riddle.::
24089::$$$message_0180_0129_0000$$$::"...Illyasviel, this is my Servant's ability."[lr]::
24090::$$$message_0180_0129_0001$$$::With a certain surety, I explain everything that's happened so far.[lr]::
24091::$$$message_0180_0129_0002$$$::Resurrecting after death. Retrying the Holy Grail War over and over.[lr]::
24092::$$$message_0180_0129_0003$$$::No, I tell her the story of how my Servant and I can't get past the fourth day, no matter how many times we repeat it.::
24093::$$$message_0180_0130_0000$$$::"...You're repeating the Holy Grail War... I see.[lr]::
24094::$$$message_0180_0130_0001$$$::That's how it feels to you... No, you're the only ones still stuck here."::
24095::$$$message_0180_0131_0000$$$::...That's an accurate way to describe it.[lr]::
24096::$$$message_0180_0131_0001$$$::From her point of view, the fifth day comes after the fourth day.[lr]::
24097::$$$message_0180_0131_0002$$$::But for us, we return to the first day.[lr]::
24098::$$$message_0180_0131_0003$$$::It's like we're getting stuck in the great river of time, occasionally climbing upstream.::
24099::$$$message_0180_0132_0000$$$::"You came here to figure this out. You want to stop the Holy Grail War and go past the fourth day."[lr]::
24100::$$$message_0180_0132_0001$$$::"Huh? N-no, I just..."[lr]::
24101::$$$message_0180_0132_0002$$$::I don't have any desire to stop the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
24102::$$$message_0180_0132_0003$$$::I just want to know why we're only limited to four days.::
24103::$$$message_0180_0133_0000$$$::"Am I wrong? What do you want to do? Do you want to keep doing this forever?[block len=6]"[lr]::
24104::$$$message_0180_0133_0001$$$::No. I just want to win this bizarre war and finish my mission.::
24105::$$$message_0180_0134_0000$$$::"Oh. Well, I could help you if you sever your pact with your Servant, but your problem is outside my jurisdiction.[lr]::
24106::$$$message_0180_0134_0001$$$::I told you I'm not part of this anymore.[lr]::
24107::$$$message_0180_0134_0002$$$::I don't feel like leaving this castle. You'll have to figure out for yourself why your Holy Grail War has become like this, Bazett."::
24108::$$$message_0180_0135_0000$$$::The girl stands.[lr]::
24109::$$$message_0180_0135_0001$$$::Illyasviel leaves the lobby, looking bored of me.::
24110::$$$message_0180_0136_0000$$$::"Good night, Bazett. If what you said is true, then you'll be going back tonight. You should stay in the castle until then. The ghost will attack if you go back into the forest.[lr]::
24111::$$$message_0180_0136_0001$$$::...The stars are pretty tonight. You should take the time to think while you're alone.[lr]::
24112::$$$message_0180_0136_0002$$$::What do you want to do? Do you truly want to fix what's wrong?"::
24113::$$$message_0180_0137_0000$$$::...I leave the wintry castle.[lr]::
24114::$$$message_0180_0137_0001$$$::I declined her offer.[lr]::
24115::$$$message_0180_0137_0002$$$::Even if that means I go into the forest and the monster kills me, I can't stay here and relax by myself.::
24116::$$$message_0180_0138_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
24117::$$$message_0180_0138_0001$$$::It's a clear night, indeed.[lr]::
24118::$$$message_0180_0138_0002$$$::I gaze up at the uncountable stars. He'd probably say something sarcastic, like, "I can count them as long as I can see them."::
24119::$$$message_0180_0139_0000$$$::"...I need to find out why this all started,[lr]::
24120::$$$message_0180_0139_0001$$$::not why it won't end after the fourth day."[lr]::
24121::$$$message_0180_0139_0002$$$::It isn't Avenger's Noble Phantasm that's turning back time.[lr]::
24122::$$$message_0180_0139_0003$$$::He said it himself...[lr]::
24123::$$$message_0180_0139_0004$$$::it's just a bonus effect of our contract.[lr]::
24124::$$$message_0180_0139_0005$$$::But what's the bonus?[lr]::
24125::$$$message_0180_0139_0006$$$::I ask myself what other than a Noble Phantasm could possibly cause such a miracle...::
24126::$$$message_0180_0140_0000$$$::...and deny the answer that comes to mind.::
24127::$$$message_0180_0141_0000$$$::"...I can't trust Avenger.[lr]::
24128::$$$message_0180_0141_0001$$$::I can only do what's in my own power."[lr]::
24129::$$$message_0180_0141_0002$$$::...That's right. Next time, I'll investigate the town while he's asleep during the day.[lr]::
24130::$$$message_0180_0141_0003$$$::Avenger says he can't operate during daytime, but I have no such restrictions.[lr]::
24131::$$$message_0180_0141_0004$$$::I've only been avoiding it, but I'm not a vampire or anything.::
24132::$$$message_0180_0142_0000$$$::"The mages in Fuyuki are Tohsaka, Matou...and Kiritsugu Emiya who survived the last war."[lr]::
24133::$$$message_0180_0142_0001$$$::That's where I should begin my search.[lr]::
24134::$$$message_0180_0142_0002$$$::I'm going to explore the town without telling my Servant.[lr]::
24135::$$$message_0180_0142_0003$$$::An ache gnaws at my chest again.[lr]::
24136::$$$message_0180_0142_0004$$$::...I wish I really couldn't trust him, deep down.[lr]::
24137::$$$message_0180_0142_0005$$$::I want to trust him, but I'm going to keep him in the dark and find out the truth.::

